.\" mazecarve.6 - the mazecarve man page
.TH MAZECARVE 6 "mazecarve 2.0.0" "Games"
.SH NAME
mazecarve \- a terminal maze generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mazecarve
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mazecarve
generates mazes in a terminal.  It is meant to be watched
rather than played: mazes can be carved live, one cell at a time, in
color, or printed to standard output.  Nothing about solving or playing
a maze is included.
.PP
The same seed always produces the same maze, in every view.
.SH MODES
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-live
Animate the maze being carved.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-infinite
Keep generating new mazes forever.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-screensaver
Live + infinite; quits on any keypress.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print
Print the finished maze to standard output and exit, without starting
the full-screen view.
.SH TIMING
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time= TIME
Seconds between animation steps (default 0.01).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wait= TIME
Seconds to pause between mazes (default 1.0).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-seed= INT
Seed, so the same maze comes back.
.SH APPEARANCE
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-type= TYPE
Maze algorithm (default backtracker).  One of backtracker, prim,
kruskal, wilson, aldous-broder, eller, growing-tree, division,
sidewinder, binary-tree, hunt-and-kill, random.
.TP
.BI \-\-style= STYLE
Wall style for the top view: dots (default, tiny . dots), texture, ascii,
unicode or block.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme= THEME
Color theme: default, forest, ocean, amber or mono.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-colors= LIST
Comma list of colors overriding the theme roles, in order:
wall,path,head,trail1,trail2,unvisited,endpoint.  Colors are names,
xterm-256 indices or #rrggbb hex.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-wall\-width= INT
Wall thickness in characters (default 1).
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-corridor= INT
Corridor width in characters (default 2).
.TP
.BI \-\-fill= PCT
Share of the terminal the maze may use (default 67).
.TP
.BI \-\-size= WxH
Fixed maze size in cells.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-message= STR
Show a message below the maze, like cbonsai.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-endpoints
Mark an entrance and an exit.
.SH VIEWS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-view= VIEW
How the maze is drawn: top (the default flat plan), iso (2:1 dimetric
isometric) or oblique (front-facing with a diagonal depth offset).  The
isometric views use a parallel projection: walls become blocks with a
top face and two side faces, drawn back to front so nearer walls hide
what is behind them.  Mazes are auto-sized to fit the terminal.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-wall\-height= INT
Wall height in rows for the iso and oblique views (default 2).  Taller
walls look more 3D but hide more of the floor; 1 is the most readable.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-rotate= INT
Which corner of the maze faces the viewer: 0, 1, 2 or 3 (90 degree
steps, default 0).
.TP
.BI \-\-shade= BOOL
Shade the three wall faces differently (top lightest, left medium,
right darkest), using the theme's wall color.  Default on.
.B \-\-no\-shade
is equivalent to \-\-shade=no.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-floor
Do not draw floor tiles in the iso/oblique views, only walls.
.TP
.BI \-\-iso\-style= STYLE
Glyph set for the iso/oblique views: ascii (/ \\ _ |), box (box drawing
and diagonals) or block (solid blocks of different density).  The live
view defaults to box on UTF-8 terminals; printed output always defaults
to plain ascii.
.SH TWEAKS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-braid= INT
Percentage of dead ends to remove (0-100).
.TP
.BI \-\-strategy= STRAT
Growing tree strategy: newest, oldest, random or mix.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-save= FILE
Save the seed and settings to FILE.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-load= FILE
Load a saved maze configuration; command line flags still win.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help text and exit.
.SH KEYS
.B q
,
.B ESC
and
.B Ctrl-C
quit; in screensaver mode any key quits.  The terminal is restored
cleanly on exit, including on SIGTERM and SIGHUP.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
mazecarve \-l                         # watch a maze carve itself
mazecarve \-l \-T wilson \-\-theme=ocean
mazecarve \-l \-S                      # screensaver
mazecarve \-p \-\-size=40x20 > maze.txt
mazecarve \-V iso \-l \-H 3             # isometric view, taller walls
mazecarve \-p \-V iso \-R 1 > maze.txt  # rotated isometric maze, printed
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM, COLORTERM
Used to work out how many colors the terminal can show.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, draw without colors.
.SH SEE ALSO
The mazecarve README, shipped with the source.
